        "testata": "France 24",
        "lingua_originale": "en",
        "titolo_orig": "Vance visits Hungary to boost Orban re-election bid",
        "testo_it": "Il vicepresidente USA JD Vance visita l'Ungheria per supportare la campagna elettorale di Viktor Orbán.",
        "priorita": "Alta",
        "id_gruppo": 4,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260407-vance-visits-hungary-to-boost-orban-re-election-bid",
        "orario": "14:44",
        "timestamp": 1775565886,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Vance visits Hungary to boost Orban re-election bid Issued on: 07/04/2026 - 14:44 Modified: 07/04/2026 - 14:46 US Vice President JD Vance arrived in Budapest to boost Viktor Orban's campaign ahead of an election that many opinion polls suggest the veteran nationalist leader will lose. Orban, a eurosceptic nationalist in power since 2010, is facing the toughest re-election bidof his career, with independent polls indicating his Fidesz party will ​lose Sunday's vote to centre-right ‌challenger Peter Magyar's Tisza party. Gunmen attack building housing Israeli Consulate in Istanbul 07/04/2026 Exiled for a drawing: The Russian father and daughter who stood up to Putin 07/04/2026 Iran calls for young people to form human chains to protect power plants 07/04/2026 California 'architect' of 19th century native American genocide, 'US govt 'funded' most of killing' 07/04/2026 Americas Trump threatens to take out Iran in 'one night' as deadline looms 07/04/2026 Middle East Manlio Graziano: 'Europe still needs the US but they know they cannot trust Americans anymore' 07/04/2026 Europe Artemis II crew start trip home after milestone-rich lunar flyby 07/04/2026 Cape Town mums patrol streets amid surge in violence 07/04/2026 French drivers choke on soaring diesel prices 07/04/2026"
